# 11g's reply to `select id, p, ns from pyo_drcp_ot order by id` on a pooled
# session (#2466): P an object (PYO_DRCP_PT: x NUMBER, label VARCHAR2(20)), NS
# a nested table (PYO_DRCP_NUMS of NUMBER), both described as type 109 with
# their type's schema and name; then the rows (1, PYO_DRCP_PT(10, 'ten'),
# PYO_DRCP_NUMS(1, 2, 3)) and (2, NULL, NULL), each object cell the native 9.2
# form's image; then the status, ORA-01403.
# Captured 2026-11-06 through tools/capture_proxy.py: seerdb's pooled session on
# Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2, the DRCP pool started. The TTC payload, without the
# packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii|
# gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
